IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `anzac-rules`

-- Protection of Word "Anzac" Act 1920 (Cth) — the encoder's tests.

§ `Tests`

#ASSERT `the Anzac penalty for` (`Anzac case` OF `in connection with a trade, business, calling or profession`, `subregulation 2(1)`) EQUALS `imprisonment for up to 12 months`
#ASSERT `the Anzac penalty for` (`Anzac case` OF `in connection with an entertainment, lottery or art union`, `subregulation 2(1)`) EQUALS `imprisonment for up to 12 months`
#ASSERT `the Anzac penalty for` (`Anzac case` OF `as the name of a private residence, boat, vehicle, or charitable or other institution, or a building connected with it`, `subregulation 2(1)`) EQUALS `imprisonment for up to 12 months`
#ASSERT `the Anzac penalty for` (`Anzac case` OF `as the name of a street, road or park`, `subregulation 3(1)`) EQUALS `imprisonment for up to 12 months`
-- a subregulation 2(1) breach by another use
#ASSERT `the Anzac penalty for` (`Anzac case` OF `another use`, `subregulation 2(1)`) EQUALS `the penalty the Regulations set, a fine of at most $1,000`
-- a street name breaching 2(1) rather than 3(1)
#ASSERT `the Anzac penalty for` (`Anzac case` OF `as the name of a street, road or park`, `subregulation 2(1)`) EQUALS `the penalty the Regulations set, a fine of at most $1,000`
#ASSERT `the Anzac penalty for` (`Anzac case` OF `in connection with a trade, business, calling or profession`, `another regulation`) EQUALS `the penalty the Regulations set, a fine of at most $1,000`
#ASSERT `the Anzac penalty for` (`Anzac case` OF `in connection with a trade, business, calling or profession`, `no breach`) EQUALS `no penalty`
